# =============================================================================
# CitOmni - INTERNAL DIRECTORY ACCESS DENIAL
#
# PURPOSE
#   Prevent direct HTTP access to internal application directories when the
#   application root is exposed as the web root.
#
# THREAT MODEL
#   - Prevent disclosure of application source code, configuration, logs,
#     cached data, dependencies, tooling, and other non-public files.
#   - Provide defense-in-depth if app-root routing or web-server configuration
#     is changed, bypassed, or misconfigured.
#   - Ensure internal directories remain non-public even when their contents
#     would otherwise be directly addressable by URL.
#
# BEHAVIOR
#   - Denies every HTTP request to this directory and its contents.
#   - Provides defense-in-depth in addition to app-root routing rules.
#
# REQUIREMENTS
#   - Apache 2.4+ with mod_authz_core.
#
# NOTES
#   - Place this file in each top-level internal application directory.
#   - Do not place it in /public.
# =============================================================================

Require all denied
